"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1657,"Mu'ammal ibn Hisham and Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, they said: Isma'il narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us - and Mu'ammal said: from Khalid al-Hadhdha' - from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Malih, who said: I went out on a dark night to the mosque for the 'Isha' prayer. When I returned, I sought to have the door opened, so my father said: ""Who is this?"" They said: ""Abu Malih."" He said: ""I have indeed seen us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of al-Hudaybiyah, and rain fell upon us that did not even wet the soles of our sandals, so the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out: 'Pray in your dwellings.'"""
